course: dictionary
lesson: 4834
title: The hutch: a home for small pets
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hutch is a wooden box or cage with a wire front, where small pets such as rabbits and guinea pigs live. Read the words around it to work out its meaning: «Ruby cleaned the hutch on Saturday, said sorry, and fed him every day after.» Cleaning and feeding show that a hutch is the pet's home, and someone must look after it.
explain: «Cages and hutches must be kept in the shade, because small animals can overheat and die quickly in the sun.» The word because tells you the reason. Shade keeps the hutch cool, so the animal stays safe. Always check your meaning by reading the whole sentence again.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. In American English, a hutch is also a cupboard with open shelves on top, for dishes. If the sentence is about animals, a hutch is the animal's home.
fact: A hutch is a wooden box or cage with a wire front.
fact: A hutch must be big enough for the animal to hop, stretch and stand up.
fact: A hutch must be kept clean and dry, with fresh water, hay and bedding.
fact: «On freezing nights small animals in hutches need a sheltered place and extra bedding.»
fact: Rabbits also need a run to exercise and a friend of their own kind.
exercise: «Maddie forgets to fill the rabbit's water bowl for two days and finds it lying still in the hutch.» What does hutch mean in this sentence? | A cupboard for dishes | *The rabbit's home, a wooden box with a wire front | A kind of food | A hot, sunny field
exercise: «Cages and hutches must be kept in the shade.» Why must a hutch be kept in the shade? | So the hutch is easier to carry | So the hutch can be painted | *So the animal does not overheat in the sun | The shade makes the water taste nicer
exercise: «On freezing nights small animals in hutches need a sheltered place and extra bedding.» Find and copy one word that means protected from wind and rain. | nights | freezing | bedding | *sheltered
test: In a pet-care lesson, what must a good hutch have? | *Room to hop and stretch, and a clean, dry floor | A wire top only, with no sides | A deep pool of water | Very small, so the pet stays warm and close
test: Besides a hutch, what else do rabbits need? | A cupboard with open shelves | A hot lamp on all day | *A run to exercise in | A glass tank with no air holes
exam: In American English, what is a hutch? | A wooden box for storing hay outside | *A cupboard with open shelves on top, for dishes | A small pet's food bowl | A wire fence round a garden
